      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a failed resize frees the context buffers and a subsequent config change recovers to a smaller resolution than `last_coded_width`x`last_coded_height`, entering this block via `retry_realloc` overwrites `cpi-\u003eexternal_resize \u003d 0` even when the next frame is a scaled inter frame. Also, if a downscale failed in the second block below, the context buffers here were never freed.\n\nConsider zeroing `cpi-\u003einitial_width` and `cpi-\u003einitial_height` before `vp9_free_context_buffers(cm)` (so `!cpi-\u003einitial_width || !cpi-\u003einitial_height` triggers reallocation on retry without needing `retry_realloc` here) and keeping `cpi-\u003eexternal_resize \u003d 1` when `cm-\u003ewidth !\u003d cpi-\u003elast_coded_width || cm-\u003eheight !\u003d cpi-\u003elast_coded_height`.",
