      "message": "When `vp9_change_config()` fails, `ctx-\u003ecfg` and `cm-\u003eprofile` have already been updated and `cm-\u003eprev_mip` / `cm-\u003elast_frame_seg_map` freed, but `if (force_key) ctx-\u003enext_frame_flags |\u003d VPX_EFLAG_FORCE_KF;` at line 924 is skipped. A subsequent recovery to the original/downscaled size (or retrying the same `cfg`, where `cfg-\u003eg_w \u003d\u003d ctx-\u003ecfg.g_w`) then leaves `force_key \u003d\u003d 0`.\n\nSet `if (force_key) ctx-\u003enext_frame_flags |\u003d VPX_EFLAG_FORCE_KF;` before calling `vp9_change_config()`, and also check `ctx-\u003ecpi-\u003erealloc_pending` in the size-change condition at line 873.",
